//! The `bottom` [CSS](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS) property participates in
//! setting the vertical position of a [positioned
//! element](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/Reference/Properties/position). This
//! `inset property` has no effect on non-positioned elements.
//!
//! Initial: auto. Inherited: no.
//! Percentages: refer to the height of the containing block.
//!
//! Keyword effects:
//! - auto: Specifies that: - for _absolutely positioned elements_, the position of the element is
//! based on the `top` property, while `height: auto` is treated as a height based on the content; or
//! if `top` is also `auto`, the element is positioned where it should vertically be positioned if it
//! were a static element. - for _relatively positioned elements_, the distance of the element from
//! its normal position is based on the `top` property; or if `top` is also `auto`, the element is
//! not moved vertically at all.
//!
//! Grammar: auto | <length-percentage> | <anchor()> | <anchor-size()>
//!
//! Specification: https://drafts.csswg.org/css-position-3/#propdef-bottom
//!
//! Author guide: https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/Reference/Properties/bottom
//!
//! Purpose and value descriptions adapted from MDN contributors (CC-BY-SA-2.5).
//!
//! Generated from @webref/css 8.7.8. Do not edit.

